## 1. Purpose

This License grants permission to use, copy, study, modify, fork, and redistribute the software known as **VELUM** (the "Software"), subject to the conditions described below.

The purpose of this License is to allow the Software to be freely used, modified, and redistributed while ensuring that the Software and Derivative Works remain freely available to end users and that the original project and its authors receive appropriate attribution.

This License does not prohibit ordinary commercial activities that are independent of the Software, nor does it prohibit the internal use of the Software by businesses or organizations.

---

## 2. Definitions

### 2.1 "Software"

"Software" means the original software, source code, compiled binaries, documentation, configuration, assets, and other materials distributed by the Copyright Holder under this License.

### 2.2 "Derivative Work"

A "Derivative Work" means any software or other work that:

- Is based upon the Software;
- Modifies or extends the Software;
- Is created from a fork or modified version of the Software;
- Is built substantially upon the Software; or
- Incorporates one or more Substantial Functional Components of the Software.

Changing, replacing, or substantially redesigning the user interface does not, by itself, prevent a work from being considered a Derivative Work.

Adding substantial original code or additional functionality also does not, by itself, prevent a work from being considered a Derivative Work.

A work that merely interacts with, communicates with, interoperates with, or is distributed alongside the Software does not become a Derivative Work solely because of such interaction.

### 2.3 "Substantial Functional Component"

A "Substantial Functional Component" means a complete or materially significant module, subsystem, feature, or functional component of the Software, regardless of the amount of source code it represents relative to the Software as a whole.

A component may be considered substantial because of its functionality, importance, independence, or role within the Software, even if it represents only a small percentage of the total source code.

For example, if the Software contains a complete video downloading module and another project incorporates that module or a substantial portion of its implementation, that component may constitute a Substantial Functional Component even if the module represents only a small portion of the Software's total codebase.

A trivial, incidental, or independently implemented piece of functionality does not become a Substantial Functional Component merely because it performs a similar function.

### 2.4 "Distribution"

"Distribution" means making the Software or a Derivative Work available to another person or organization, whether by download, physical media, online distribution, application store, package repository, preinstallation, or any other means.

### 2.5 "Mandatory Payment"

"Mandatory Payment" means any payment, purchase, subscription, fee, license charge, access charge, or other financial consideration that a user is required to provide as a condition of obtaining, downloading, installing, accessing, configuring, activating, or using the Software or a Derivative Work.

### 2.6 "Commercial Offering"

A "Commercial Offering" means a product, service, hardware device, software product, hosted solution, enterprise solution, or other offering provided to third parties for commercial consideration where the Software or a Derivative Work forms part of, materially contributes to, or is provided as a component of that offering.

