## 9. Commercial Products and Services

The Software may not be incorporated into or distributed as part of a Commercial Offering without prior written permission from the Copyright Holder.

Examples requiring prior permission include:

- Pre-installing the Software on computers or other hardware sold commercially;
- Bundling the Software with commercial hardware;
- Including the Software as part of a commercial software product;
- Providing the Software as an integrated component of a commercial service;
- Incorporating the Software into an enterprise product or commercial solution;
- Providing the Software as a component of a product or service sold to customers;
- Distributing the Software to customers as part of a commercial offering.

The fact that the Software itself is provided to the customer without a separate charge does not by itself make such use permitted.

The Copyright Holder may grant separate permission, additional terms, or a separate commercial license for such uses.

