## 10. Attribution

Any public Distribution of the Software or a Derivative Work must retain appropriate attribution to the original project.

At a minimum, the following information must be preserved:

**Original Project:** VELUM  
**Original Author / Copyright Holder:** Eduardo Lemus Laguna  
**Original Repository:** https://github.com/LaloSoftware/project-velum

A public Derivative Work must clearly indicate that it is based on or derived from the original project.

An acceptable attribution may be presented as:

> This project is based on VELUM, originally created by Eduardo Lemus Laguna.  
> Original project: https://github.com/LaloSoftware/project-velum

The attribution must be reasonably visible and accessible to users of the Derivative Work.

You may not intentionally remove, obscure, or misrepresent the original project's attribution.

